From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] ldi_vnode: synchronous I/O waits for its buf before freeing it

buf_strategy_vnode() issues a synchronous I/O (no b_iodone) with
VNOP_STRATEGY() and then calls ldi_vnode_io_intr(), which frees the buf,
but VNOP_STRATEGY() only starts the I/O. When the device completed it,
buf_biodone() worked on a freed buf, and under the OpenZFS test suite
(zpool_import, zpool_scrub, P3-01 checkpoint 2) xnu panicked in
free_io_buf() ("bufs_iobufinuse < 0"). It now waits with buf_biowait()
first, as spec and file system code does for a synchronous buf.

Rebase-risk: low
---
diff --git a/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/ldi_vnode.c b/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/ldi_vnode.c
--- a/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/ldi_vnode.c
+++ b/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/ldi_vnode.c
@@ -622,6 +622,16 @@
 
 	/* For synchronous IO, call completion */
 	if (lbp->b_iodone == NULL) {
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+		/*
+		 * VNOP_STRATEGY() only starts the I/O: wait for it before
+		 * ldi_vnode_io_intr() frees the buf, or the device's
+		 * completion finds it freed (free_io_buf: bufs_iobufinuse
+		 * < 0). buf_biowait()'s error is the buf's, which
+		 * ldi_vnode_io_intr() copies out.
+		 */
+		(void) buf_biowait(bp);
+#endif
 		ldi_vnode_io_intr(bp, (void*)lbp);
 	}
 
